From 524d00c3fa85ea7b2c96242ec03eb9b45dfa7630 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Apr 2026 18:13:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: unified fade transition system across all windows
 and views
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Core/WindowFader.cs (new):
- Central static helper — all timing constants in one place
- FadeIn(window)           — 0→1 opacity, 200ms, CubicEase out
- FadeOut(window, action)  — current→0, 150ms, CubicEase in, callback on complete
- FadeRestore(window)      — used after WindowState restores from Minimized, 220ms
- FadeMinimize(window)     — fades to 0, then minimizes, resets opacity to 1
- AnimateViewTransitionAsync(element) — 110ms fade-out + 200ms fade-in for ContentControl

MainWindow.xaml.cs:
- Startup: Opacity=0, FadeIn on Loaded
- Minimize button: FadeMinimize instead of instant state change
- Restore from taskbar: StateChanged triggers FadeRestore
- Close button / X: OnClosing intercepts, FadeOut → Hide (to tray), reset opacity=1
- View switching: replaced bespoke DoubleAnimationUsingKeyFrames with
  WindowFader.AnimateViewTransitionAsync for cleaner code
- Removed unused _settingsPath field duplication

TrayPopupWindow.xaml.cs:
- IsVisibleChanged: FadeIn on every Show (160ms)
- Deactivated: FadeOut → Hide (120ms), reset opacity=1
- Navigation clicks: instant hide (no delay before main window appears)

AdminLoginWindow.xaml.cs:
- Opacity=0 + FadeIn on Loaded (200ms)
- Closing: cancel → FadeOut → re-close via _animatingClose guard
- Minimize: FadeMinimize

